The file patches the real Go source of math/big/intconv.go.

go of the package math/big.

The real file writes the message of an unknown verb with fmt.Fprintf and
fmt.Fprint. The 2 functions take an io.Writer, and the flow of stage 3 then
gives the call the group of each Write method of the program. That group holds
a Write that blocks, thus each program that formats a value of this package
loses a //gart:sync position. This file writes the same bytes through the
fmt.State that the caller gives. Read the section "The method group of an
interface call" of docs/parity.md.

